                <pb facs="0250" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/601: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-15T18:00:00-04:00">March 15, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 15—5:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Government has under consideration new proposal affecting adversely, probably
                    by indefinite moratorium, 60 peso charge and restoring old export tax for
                    benefit of Government finances. New proposal may affect foreign interests more
                    seriously than former proposal referred to in despatch No. 1377, February
                        8th<anchor n="52" xml:id="d146-f1"/> and other communications on the same
                    subject. I have already talked with the Foreign Minister and as before am using
                    my good offices to prevent an open break.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
